(4210520, 605734, 61577, '<td valign="top">a little out of focus. Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'a little out of focus. Good luck in the challenge.', '2007-11-01 00:56:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(4210524, 598019, 8522, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot, doesn''t really work for me unfortunately for a few reasons...<br/>The floor is not a good texture for this shot, it just looks like cheap laminate that happened to be on your living room floor rather than an inspiring surface with a texture you knew had to feature in your shot.<br/>The composition doesn''t work for me at all, she feels far too high in the frame with too much negative space at the bottom. I''m not sure how I feel about her head at the bottom right of the shot... the head really needs to be the focus which is better achieved at the top left of the frame. Because the bottom is the highest part of the shot, and it''s very light, the eye is confused about whether this is the focal point. If there was more detail, it could be, but it''s overexposed and burnt out. Besides, your model has a lovely face and expression, and I feel that this should be the focal point. The lighting doesn''t quite work... like I said, the bottom is burnt out which is a shame as the rest of the body is backlit quite nicely. The head needs better lighting though, and the shadow cast by the head is not good at all. A question that pops into my mind is why you used the rug? I feel that you could have made more of this, it''s a little kitsch and you could have had some fun with that. You clearly have a great model and I feel that this photo has tried to conjure a 70s glamour feel which just doesn''t work on a cheap looking floor with a cheap naff rug (sorry!), I think your model deserves much better surroundings if you want this shot to look classy rather than cheap. Her expression is lovely and heartfelt, and you need to reflect this with everything around her.</td>', 'Interesting shot, doesn''t really work for me unfortunately for a few reasons...The floor is not a good texture for this shot, it just looks like cheap laminate that happened to be on your living room floor rather than an inspiring surface with a texture you knew had to feature in your shot.The composition doesn''t work for me at all, she feels far too high in the frame with too much negative space at the bottom. I''m not sure how I feel about her head at the bottom right of the shot... the head really needs to be the focus which is better achieved at the top left of the frame. Because the bottom is the highest part of the shot, and it''s very light, the eye is confused about whether this is the focal point. If there was more detail, it could be, but it''s overexposed and burnt out. Besides, your model has a lovely face and expression, and I feel that this should be the focal point. The lighting doesn''t quite work... like I said, the bottom is burnt out which is a shame as the rest of the body is backlit quite nicely. The head needs better lighting though, and the shadow cast by the head is not good at all. A question that pops into my mind is why you used the rug? I feel that you could have made more of this, it''s a little kitsch and you could have had some fun with that. You clearly have a great model and I feel that this photo has tried to conjure a 70s glamour feel which just doesn''t work on a cheap looking floor with a cheap naff rug (sorry!), I think your model deserves much better surroundings if you want this shot to look classy rather than cheap. Her expression is lovely and heartfelt, and you need to reflect this with everything around her.', '2007-11-01 00:57:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(4210531, 605686, 45631, '<td valign="top">This is a nice sharp shot with lovely colors but I think that crop is rather severe.</td>', 'This is a nice sharp shot with lovely colors but I think that crop is rather severe.', '2007-11-01 00:58:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(4210537, 600891, 8522, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot! I wish there was a tad more detail in the face, at the moment, the stripes of the shorts are the sharpest part of the shot which tries to make it the point of focus. Otherwise, you could blur the detail there which would allow the eye to focus more naturally on the face. I like the tilt. Red umbrella works well.</td>', 'Lovely shot! I wish there was a tad more detail in the face, at the moment, the stripes of the shorts are the sharpest part of the shot which tries to make it the point of focus. Otherwise, you could blur the detail there which would allow the eye to focus more naturally on the face. I like the tilt. Red umbrella works well.', '2007-11-01 00:59:46.000000', NULL, 1),
