(4220442, 606889, 23484, '<td valign="top">Cool shot. Very halloween looking.</td>', 'Cool shot. Very halloween looking.', '2007-11-04 13:43:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(4220502, 600198, 39850, '<td valign="top">See, that''s the trouble with putting an image like this in a Free Study where you will get voters who automatically see an image like this and are so stuck in a ''small world'' box .... that they think this must be either photoshopped, ''copied from Hubble'' or could not be achieved in a single exposure (re the validation (which in this case is a good little ''badge'' to have here)).  Having said that, I <i>do</i> wish I knew enough about astronomy to comment on this from a scientific point of view (and also photographic, because these images require a developed skill set (and equipment)).  However I <i>can</i> comment on the aesthetics and, whilst this is of course a beautiful subject, the colors look slightly washed and the black is not as black as I''d like to see, especially to make the galaxy ''pop'' more.  I ''guess'' it is fairly text book for this galaxy, and it is difficult to make ''creative'' suggestions for such an image.  The only thing I wonder about is, whether a variation in composition and/or framing might give this an edge over other similar images.  I do hope we get an Astronomy Challenge.  And, I hope one day to be able to take/create an image like this.  Until then I always admire the images of those that do and have some appreciation of the work involved and knowledge required.  Hope that all makes sense.  Giving this a 7, but one of the most difficult images I''ve had to score at DPC.  Up to 8 from 7 - because of the difficulty involved with this <i>single</i> exposure.</td>', 'See, that''s the trouble with putting an image like this in a Free Study where you will get voters who automatically see an image like this and are so stuck in a ''small world'' box .... that they think this must be either photoshopped, ''copied from Hubble'' or could not be achieved in a single exposure (re the validation (which in this case is a good little ''badge'' to have here)).  Having said that, I do wish I knew enough about astronomy to comment on this from a scientific point of view (and also photographic, because these images require a developed skill set (and equipment)).  However I can comment on the aesthetics and, whilst this is of course a beautiful subject, the colors look slightly washed and the black is not as black as I''d like to see, especially to make the galaxy ''pop'' more.  I ''guess'' it is fairly text book for this galaxy, and it is difficult to make ''creative'' suggestions for such an image.  The only thing I wonder about is, whether a variation in composition and/or framing might give this an edge over other similar images.  I do hope we get an Astronomy Challenge.  And, I hope one day to be able to take/create an image like this.  Until then I always admire the images of those that do and have some appreciation of the work involved and knowledge required.  Hope that all makes sense.  Giving this a 7, but one of the most difficult images I''ve had to score at DPC.  Up to 8 from 7 - because of the difficulty involved with this single exposure.', '2007-11-04 14:38:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(4220514, 607228, 63269, '<td valign="top">Beautiful colors and tones here!</td>', 'Beautiful colors and tones here!', '2007-11-04 14:52:20.000000', NULL, 1);
