(4231429, 602492, 72670, '<td valign="top">No Surprise here! Congratulations on another spectacular shot. What is surprising is that there were 4''s in the voting. But I guess it didn''t matter. Nice work!</td>', 'No Surprise here! Congratulations on another spectacular shot. What is surprising is that there were 4''s in the voting. But I guess it didn''t matter. Nice work!', '2007-11-08 08:17:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231432, 602492, 66348, '<td valign="top">Wow just incredible image bro. You captured exactly what you were going for here. I ditto what MAK said. Steak dinner for the Mrs... Congrats on the Ribb.</td>', 'Wow just incredible image bro. You captured exactly what you were going for here. I ditto what MAK said. Steak dinner for the Mrs... Congrats on the Ribb.', '2007-11-08 08:19:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231433, 606318, 48201, '<td valign="top">The comments are interesting.  I understand what you guys mean and I agree as far as the shot itself, but I wonder if you have shot much racing from the fan side of the fence?<br/> <br/>I had very little choice about background because not many spots around the track are close enough to get a shot at speed, aren''t crowded with people, or have fencing blocking the view.<br/> <br/>As for the composition, these guys are going over 100 mph.  I''ve been going to this race and taking photos for 9 years and it is really tough to put everything together at once.  I actually only cropped out the background a bit, the back of the car was cut off in the original and there wasn''t anymore space in front of the car.<br/> <br/>Anyway, just a bit of explanation.  Like I said I get what you mean and I agree, but doing those things in the situation I was shooting in is pert'' near impossible.  Maybe I also didn''t choose my best shot to enter due to lack of time.  Now that the challenge is over I''ll put a few others up.</td>', 'The comments are interesting.  I understand what you guys mean and I agree as far as the shot itself, but I wonder if you have shot much racing from the fan side of the fence? I had very little choice about background because not many spots around the track are close enough to get a shot at speed, aren''t crowded with people, or have fencing blocking the view. As for the composition, these guys are going over 100 mph.  I''ve been going to this race and taking photos for 9 years and it is really tough to put everything together at once.  I actually only cropped out the background a bit, the back of the car was cut off in the original and there wasn''t anymore space in front of the car. Anyway, just a bit of explanation.  Like I said I get what you mean and I agree, but doing those things in the situation I was shooting in is pert'' near impossible.  Maybe I also didn''t choose my best shot to enter due to lack of time.  Now that the challenge is over I''ll put a few others up.', '2007-11-08 08:19:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4231435, 607381, 62906, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot, it definitely has the minimalist Zen factor going on.  It''s not too dark at all for me but, I can see every block on the b/w gradient scale so, who knows about some of the others.  Anyway, I dig it.</td>', 'I like this a lot, it definitely has the minimalist Zen factor going on.  It''s not too dark at all for me but, I can see every block on the b/w gradient scale so, who knows about some of the others.  Anyway, I dig it.', '2007-11-08 08:21:17.000000', NULL, 0),
