(4499998, 605044, 70828, '<td valign="top">It was a gift given moment that had to be captured.<br/> <br/>ABSOFREAKINGLUTELY! Gorgeous capture! Congratulations ... that is an image that your family will cherish for a very very very long time, methinks.<br/> <br/>The fact that the little girl takes up such a small part of the frame but is so THERE blows me away. The whole thing is just magical. It may have been candid but you obviously saw the potential and WOW ... What a result!</td>', 'It was a gift given moment that had to be captured. ABSOFREAKINGLUTELY! Gorgeous capture! Congratulations ... that is an image that your family will cherish for a very very very long time, methinks. The fact that the little girl takes up such a small part of the frame but is so THERE blows me away. The whole thing is just magical. It may have been candid but you obviously saw the potential and WOW ... What a result!', '2008-02-20 05:38:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4506202, 603505, 5792, '<td valign="top">A well conceived toned image. Very moody and mysterious. Good perspective, composition and framing. The eyes give the viewer plenty to think about.<br/> <br/>Realizing it is high contrast, there are a couple slightly overexposed areas like the bridge of the nose, some of the makeup on the forehead and a couple other spots you could correct. One thing I like to do for that is use a very low opacity, feathered brush to clone just a tiny bit of detail into those areas from somewhere else that closely matches what should be there. Should you try it you may be amazed how absolutely natural the result looks.</td>', 'A well conceived toned image. Very moody and mysterious. Good perspective, composition and framing. The eyes give the viewer plenty to think about. Realizing it is high contrast, there are a couple slightly overexposed areas like the bridge of the nose, some of the makeup on the forehead and a couple other spots you could correct. One thing I like to do for that is use a very low opacity, feathered brush to clone just a tiny bit of detail into those areas from somewhere else that closely matches what should be there. Should you try it you may be amazed how absolutely natural the result looks.', '2008-02-22 02:52:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4506676, 607462, 17203, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Dseale:</b></div><hr/><i> Why do you think the voters didn''t like this? You got mostly all positive comments and a 6+ score... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I dunno... something about 109th place just feels less than stellar. That big ol'' 6 bar on the graph translates as, "Nice, but so what?"</td>', 'Originally posted by Dseale: Why do you think the voters didn''t like this? You got mostly all positive comments and a 6+ score...  I dunno... something about 109th place just feels less than stellar. That big ol'' 6 bar on the graph translates as, "Nice, but so what?"', '2008-02-22 09:30:08.000000', NULL, 0),
